Project Planning Phase
PocketSmart AI: Your Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant

Project Planning Phase

1. Introduction

The Planning Phase defines how the PocketSmart AI project will be developed, what resources are required, how the work will be divided, and when each activity will be completed. The main goal is to create an AI-powered assistant that helps users manage their budget, track expenses, save money, and receive personalized recommendations.

2. Project Objectives

The main objectives of PocketSmart AI are:

To help users create and manage a personal budget.

To record and categorize daily expenses.

To analyze income and spending patterns.

To provide AI-based financial recommendations.

To identify unnecessary or excessive spending.

To help users set savings goals.

To provide a simple and user-friendly interface.

To generate useful summaries and reports.


3. Project Scope

Included:

User registration/login.

Income and expense entry.

Expense categorization.

Monthly budget creation.

Budget monitoring.

Savings goal management.

AI-based recommendations.

Spending analysis.

Dashboard with charts and summaries.


Not Included:

Direct access to bank accounts.

Actual money transfers.

Investment or stock trading.

Professional financial advice.


4. Proposed Technology Stack

Component	Technology

Frontend	HTML, CSS, JavaScript
Backend	Python
Framework	Flask
Database	SQLite / MySQL
AI	Google Gemini API
Charts	Chart.js
Development Tool	VS Code
Version Control	Git & GitHub


5. Major Modules

1. User Management Module
Handles registration and login.


2. Budget Management Module
Allows users to set monthly spending limits.


3. Expense Tracking Module
Records expenses with amount, date, and category.


4. Income Management Module
Records and manages different sources of income.


5. AI Recommendation Module
Uses spending information to generate personalized suggestions.


6. Savings Goal Module
Helps users create and monitor savings targets.


7. Dashboard & Report Module
Displays spending summaries, charts, budget status, and savings information.



